#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Cowpens: South Carolina, 17 January 1781.  A sample game for the
Grognard engine.

Daniel Morgan has a thousand men, half of them militia, in a cattle
pasture with a river at his back.  Banastre Tarleton has marched all
night to catch him and attacks at sunrise.  Morgan has told the
militia exactly what to do: fire two volleys, then fall back behind the
Continentals on the rise.  Play either side against the computer, or
against a friend at the same screen.

Run it with ./cowpens (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.cowpens.json.  ./cowpens --selftest checks the map and
plays a game between two computer players.
"""

